  "knownLimitations": [
    "Prong placement is not cleft- or tip-aware; a prong may sit at the cleft.",
    "PRE-EXISTING, NOT SHAPE-SPECIFIC: this case records productionIsFullyConnected = false. The band sits 0.0681mm from basket_support and 0.1112mm from prongs, so the head floats above the band rather than touching it. This is a function of the stone FOOTPRINT, not of the heart shape: a round stone of diameter 8.0mm - a capability since Sprint 2 - reproduces the identical distances, and a princess 8x7.5 is already at 0.0378mm. The threshold sits near a 7.5mm footprint. Sprint 20 did not introduce this; its wider shape coverage surfaced it. Recorded here rather than avoided by choosing a smaller stone, so the baseline documents real geometry. See docs/bible/22-stone-v2/code-mapping-and-gaps.md."
  ],
